# Entity mapping: every attribute has one explicit owner.
mapping=[
 ('repair','리더십 특징 비교','Transformational leaders inspire a shared vision and encourage innovation. Transactional leaders use rewards for completed work and correct mistakes. Servant leaders put employee needs first and support personal development.',['Transformational','Transactional','Servant'],[('공유 비전과 혁신','Transformational'),('보상과 실수 교정','Transactional'),('직원 필요와 성장','Servant')]),
 ('repair','기억 체계','Working memory holds information briefly for an ongoing task. Episodic memory stores personally experienced events. Semantic memory stores general facts and word meanings.',['Working','Episodic','Semantic'],[('진행 중인 과제의 짧은 보관','Working'),('개인적으로 겪은 사건','Episodic'),('일반 지식과 단어 의미','Semantic')]),
 ('practice','수분 운반 구조','Xylem moves water from roots toward leaves. Phloem distributes sugars produced by photosynthesis. Stomata are pores that regulate gas exchange and water loss.',['Xylem','Phloem','Stomata'],[('당 분배','Phloem'),('기공을 통한 기체 교환','Stomata'),('뿌리에서 잎으로 물 이동','Xylem')]),
 ('practice','미술 보존 검사','Infrared imaging can reveal underdrawings beneath paint. X-ray imaging reveals dense materials and internal damage. Ultraviolet light can help identify later surface varnish repairs.',['Infrared','X-ray','Ultraviolet'],[('안료 밑의 밑그림','Infrared'),('표면 바니시의 후대 보수','Ultraviolet'),('밀도가 높은 내부 재료','X-ray')]),
 ('transfer','기상 관측 도구','A ceilometer uses a light beam to estimate cloud-base height. A disdrometer records raindrop size and speed. A pyranometer measures solar radiation reaching a surface. Each instrument answers a different weather question.',['Ceilometer','Disdrometer','Pyranometer'],[('강수 입자의 크기와 속도','Disdrometer'),('지표에 도달한 태양 복사','Pyranometer'),('구름 밑면의 높이','Ceilometer')]),
 ('transfer','도시 생태 측정','Camera traps photograph passing animals. Acoustic sensors record animal calls. Environmental DNA sampling detects traces of genetic material in water or soil. Researchers combine them because an animal may leave a genetic trace without appearing in a photograph.',['Camera trap','Acoustic sensor','Environmental DNA'],[('울음소리 기록','Acoustic sensor'),('물과 흙의 유전 물질 흔적','Environmental DNA'),('지나가는 동물의 사진','Camera trap')]),
 ('transfer','열 저장 방식','Sensible heat storage changes a material’s temperature without changing its phase. Latent heat storage uses a phase change, such as melting. Thermochemical storage uses a reversible chemical reaction.',['Sensible','Latent','Thermochemical'],[('가역 화학 반응','Thermochemical'),('상태 변화 없이 온도 변화','Sensible'),('녹는 것과 같은 상변화','Latent')])]
for role,title,p,entities,attrs in mapping:
 add('B',role,title,'mapping',passage=p,prompt='각 특징을 설명한 대상과 연결하세요.',entities=entities,attributes=[{'text':a,'entity':b} for a,b in attrs],correctAnswer={a:b for a,b in attrs},evidence=p,explanation='특징의 주어를 확인하면 각 대상에 하나씩 대응합니다. 다른 대상의 정확한 특징도 질문의 대상이 다르면 오답입니다.',hint='대상마다 동사와 목적어를 한 묶음으로 적고, 특징을 다른 대상으로 옮기지 마세요.')
# Synthetic audio only for newly authored passages; original TPO audio remains unavailable.
listening=[
 ('repair','실험실 예약 변경','Mina: I booked Lab A for Friday. Leo: Lab A will be repaired that day. Please cancel that booking, reserve Lab C, and then email our group the new location. Mina: I have already canceled Lab A. I will reserve Lab C next.','What will Mina do next?',{'A':'Cancel Lab A','B':'Reserve Lab C','C':'Start repairing Lab A'},'B','I have already canceled Lab A. I will reserve Lab C next.',[('Lab A 예약 취소',1),('Lab C 예약',2),('팀에 새 장소 전달',3)]),
 ('repair','제안의 기능','Nora: The hall is too noisy for the interview. Ravi: Why don’t we use the small room upstairs? Nora: Good idea. I will check whether it is free.','What is Ravi doing?',{'A':'Suggesting a quieter location','B':'Asking why an interview was canceled','C':'Reporting that the small room is occupied'},'A','Why don’t we use the small room upstairs?',None),
 ('practice','강의 주제 회상','Today we will examine how wetlands reduce flood damage. Their soils absorb water, vegetation slows its movement, and channels spread it over a wider area. A single reed species is only one example. These processes together explain why removing wetlands can increase flood risk.','What is the main topic?',{'A':'The classification of a single reed species','B':'The cost of constructing channels','C':'Several ways wetlands reduce flood damage'},'C','Their soils absorb water, vegetation slows its movement, and channels spread it',None),
 ('practice','버스 탑승 순서','The station moved the airport bus stop from Gate 2 to Gate 6. Passengers must first collect a boarding ticket at the indoor desk, then wait at Gate 6. You can buy a ticket online, but you still need to collect the boarding slip at the desk.','Where should passengers wait after collecting the slip?',{'A':'Gate 6','B':'Gate 2','C':'At the airport desk'},'A','then wait at Gate 6',None),
 ('transfer','시료 분석 순서','The water samples have already been filtered. Before we can run the chemical test, the bottles must be labeled. After testing, enter the results into the shared table. Please label the bottles now; the technician will handle the test.','What should the listener do now?',{'A':'Filter the samples again','B':'Enter results before testing','C':'Label the bottles'},'C','Please label the bottles now',[('병에 라벨 붙이기',1),('화학 검사',2),('결과 표 입력',3)]),
 ('transfer','회의 요청','Elena: The draft budget is ready, but I am not sure about the equipment estimates. Could you review those figures before tomorrow’s meeting? Sam: Certainly. I will send you my comments tonight.','What does Elena ask Sam to do?',{'A':'Postpone the meeting','B':'Check the equipment estimates','C':'Write the entire budget from scratch'},'B','Could you review those figures before tomorrow’s meeting?',None),
 ('transfer','학술 강의 구조','Early radio telescopes used a single large dish. Later arrays combined signals from many smaller dishes. Today we will compare how those two designs balance sensitivity and image detail. The famous mountain observatory is one example of an array, but our focus is the design trade-off.','What will the speaker mainly discuss?',{'A':'The location of a mountain observatory','B':'The career of a radio astronomer','C':'Trade-offs between two radio telescope designs'},'C','compare how those two designs balance sensitivity and image detail',None)]
for role,title,p,question,opts,key,evidence,timeline in listening:
 add('C',role,title,'listening',passage=p,prompt=question,options=opts,correctAnswer=key,evidence=evidence,explanation='질문이 묻는 기능·주제·현재 행동을 원문 표현과 연결한다. 이미 한 일이나 한 세부 사례를 정답으로 확대하지 않는다.',timeline=[{'text':t,'order':order} for t,order in timeline] if timeline else None,audioType='synthetic',audioLabel='Synthetic Practice Audio · 직접 제작 연습',recallMode='WHO / WHAT / WHERE / WHY / NEXT ACTION' if ':' in p else 'TOPIC / KEY POINTS / CONCLUSION',hint='이미 끝난 일, 지금 요청하는 일, 다음 단계를 나눠 보세요. 강의는 예시보다 공통 주제를 회상하세요.')
